gametitle=Musashi - Samurai Legend (NTSC-U) SLUS-20983 675CEB8F

// PCSX2 bundles a [Widescreen 16:9] patch for this same serial+CRC inside
// resources/patches.zip. It is NOT reproduced here: PCSX2 loads the bundled
// entry and any loose file and merges them, de-duplicating by group name
// ("Skipped loading patch 'Widescreen 16:9' since a patch with a duplicate
// name was already loaded"), so the bundled group keeps working on its own.
// Only use a group name already present in patches.zip if you mean to shadow it.

// CDeFocusPrim is a camera-distance defocus pass that runs during ordinary
// gameplay (flags=0, near=30.0, far=200.0). It draws layered translucent copies
// offset along a camera-relative direction, so at native resolution the offsets
// are sub-pixel and read as softness, while at 3x-4x internal resolution they
// separate into visible ghosting. It is not a true depth-of-field: it softens
// the 2D HUD too, which is how you can tell it is a full-frame pass.
// CGPrim::disp (0x0010AC58) skips a prim entirely when its virtual calcZ returns
// 0xF0000000, so returning that sentinel is the engine's own "do not draw" path.
// calcZ__12CDeFocusPrim (0x002D6438) is `jr ra ; move v0,zero` and is reachable
// only through _vt$12CDeFocusPrim+0x2c -- no other caller in the image.
[Remove Blur]
author=heavyjam
description=Removes the always-on defocus pass that softens the whole frame, including the HUD. Biggest win on distant geometry. Measured 1.31x edge detail on background, 1.14x on the HUD.
patch=1,EE,002D643C,word,3C02F000

// CBlurPrim is the layered radial/zoom smear used by in-game cutscenes and some
// events. It is dormant during normal play (kind=0 -> zero-size packet) and only
// turns on for those scenes (observed kind=1, rate=4, color=0x0a808080).
// Same mechanism and same uniqueness: calcZ__9CBlurPrim (0x002D65A8) is
// `jr ra ; move v0,zero`, reachable only through _vt$9CBlurPrim+0x2c.
// This one is a deliberate artistic effect -- enable only if you would rather
// have a clean image than the intended smear.
[No Motion Blur]
author=heavyjam
description=Removes the radial/zoom smear used in in-game cutscenes. Optional: it is an intentional effect, but it ghosts heavily at raised internal resolutions.
patch=1,EE,002D65AC,word,3C02F000
